ion-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS for each answer.</p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>GIVING A SPEECH</strong></p><p><strong>Reasons for nervousness</strong></p><ul><li>Lecturers often feel more nervous if the speech is <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t2-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> .</li><li>Many think that the ability to make a good public speaking is <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t2-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> , while in fact it is a skill that can be learned by anyone.</li></ul><p><strong>How to prepare a quality speech</strong></p><ul><li>The audience will only remember the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t2-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> sentence of a speech.</li><li>Ensure that your speech is <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t2-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> .</li></ul><p><strong>Do's and Don'ts</strong></p><ul><li>× Don't start your speech until audience is <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t2-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> .</li><li>✓ You can make your main ideas or notes on cards or a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t2-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> .</li><li>× You do not need to write down the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t2-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> speech.</li><li>✓ You can just write <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t2-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> ideas.</li><li>✓ Remember to <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t2-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> yourself to see how long your speech will be.</li><li>× Don't just <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t2-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> a script.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/recent_actual_test_2_academic_listening_test_2_4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-practice-source-2-t2-l-q1","part_id":"en-practice-source-2-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-practice-source-2-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"Elsinore","correct_answer_variants":["Elsinore"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3126675_1","order_index":1,"points":1},{"id":"en-practice-source-2-t2-l-q2","part_id":"en-practice-source-2-t2-l-p1","group_i